@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Data Privacy & Security";
}

<div class="container-xl px-3 px-md-4 py-5">
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="d-inline-block text-uppercase fw-bold small text-muted mb-1" style="letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.75rem;">TRUST &amp; TRANSPARENCY</span>
            <h1 class="font-serif text-dark mb-2" style="font-size: 2.25rem;">Data Privacy &amp; Security Architecture</h1>
            <p class="text-muted">How customer product assets, purchase proofs, and service histories are protected.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-card p-4 p-md-5 mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-shield-check text-forest me-2"></i>Customer Ownership &amp; Data Isolation</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small">
                Product purchases, warranty dates, and service tickets are strictly private to the authenticated customer account. Every database query enforces authenticated ownership filters (`UserId == CurrentUserId`), preventing horizontal privilege escalation or unauthorized record inspection.
            </p>

            <hr class="my-4" style="border-color: var(--pc-stone) !important;" />

            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-lock text-forest me-2"></i>Protected Invoice Storage</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small">
                Uploaded proof-of-purchase receipts (PDF, JPG, PNG) are stored in secure physical file directories located strictly outside the public web root (`Uploads/Invoices/`). Direct URL traversal is impossible due to randomized cryptographic GUID identifiers. Files are streamed exclusively through authorized controller actions that verify customer ownership prior to transmitting bytes.
            </p>

            <hr class="my-4" style="border-color: var(--pc-stone) !important;" />

            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-key text-forest me-2"></i>Credential Security &amp; Identity</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small">
                User passwords are protected with ASP.NET Core Identity utilizing salted PBKDF2 hashing. Interactive sessions are maintained through encrypted HTTP-only cookies, and external REST API integrations rely on signed HMAC-SHA256 JWT Bearer tokens.
            </p>

            <hr class="my-4" style="border-color: var(--pc-stone) !important;" />

            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-forest me-2"></i>State Machine Integrity</h2>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                Service request progressions are strictly governed by an immutable finite state machine (`ServiceRequestWorkflowService`). Every status modification produces an append-only audit trail capturing previous state, new state, technician remarks, actor credentials, and UTC timestamps.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-stone">
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i> Return to Homepage
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
